A cramped office at the Admiralty. Charts on every wall. The ADMIRAL stamps papers without reading them. A bell rings; MORDECAI enters with a hat in his hands.

ADMIRAL
Finch! Good. Saltmarsh light. Too old, too dear, too far from anywhere. Close it.

MORDECAI
Close it, sir? The light, or the town?

ADMIRAL
(stamping)
The light. The town can do as it likes. Go and look at it, write that it is hopeless, and come home by Friday.

MORDECAI
And if it isn’t hopeless?

ADMIRAL
Everything is hopeless by Friday, Finch. That is what Fridays are for.

VOICE
(off)
The coach for Saltmarsh!

The ADMIRAL waves him out. MORDECAI goes. The stamping continues into the dark.

ALL
(off, a sea shanty, distant)
Haul away, haul away home.

> BLACKOUT.
